    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (**BUILD SUCCESS**, 1 test \u2014 the only test class in the project). The acceptance test exercises the real path (create owner \u2192 `saveOwner` \u2192 `generate` \u2192 `countByCity`), so the Spring Data derived `countByCity` query is confirmed working at runtime.\n\n## Summary\n\nChanged the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (global sequence) to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a per-city sequence.\n\n**`CustomerCodeGenerator`** (`service/CustomerCodeGenerator.java`) \u2014 the one place that owns this logic:\n- `generate()` now prepends the city prefix and uses `ownerRepository.countByCity(owner.getCity()) + 1` for the sequence.\n- Generalized the private `prefix(...)` helper (previously `prefix(lastName)`) so the identical \"upper-cased first three letters\" rule is reused for both city and last name rather than duplicated.\n\n**`OwnerRepository`** \u2014 added a `countByCity(String)` method, implemented in each concrete repository so the interface stays satisfiable across all profiles:\n- `springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository` \u2014 derived automatically from the method name (same as the existing `count()`).\n- `jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl` \u2014 JPQL count with a `city` parameter.\n- `jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl` \u2014 `SELECT COUNT(*) ... WHERE city = :city`.\n\n**Derived value** \u2014 `Owner.getMembershipNumber()` embeds the full `customerCode` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), so it rebuilds on the new format automatically; I only refreshed its stale doc example.\n\n**Docs** \u2014 updated the `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` descriptions and examples in `openapi.yml` to match the new format.\n\nEach piece stayed in its natural home: format construction in the generator, persistence counting in the repositories, and the derived membership number untouched apart from documentation.",
